You sense the presence of spoilers.--More--

	You may have noticed that figurines are represented by the
symbol '(', which is used for tools.  This is not a coincidence.  If
you apply it, it will transform into a creature of the appropriate
type.  Whether it is belligerent, tame, or peaceful depends upon its
blessed/cursed statue, among other things.  I believe a blessed
figurine will always turn into a tame creature, and a cursed one will
always be belligerent.  I'm not sure of that, though.

	Statues are another thing entirely.  These can be broken up
into rocks with either a pick-axe or a wand of (digging?  I've never
tested this.)  Some of them are hollow and contain spellbooks.  The
chance that one will contain a book is based on the level at which you
found it, with one exception.  Statues created by a cockatrice or the
Medusa will never contain spellbooks.  There is a trick here that will
enable one to get many, many spellbooks.

You sense the presence of a possible abuse of the game.--More--

	Ingredients:
	1 cockatrice corpse
	1 pair of gloves
	1 pick-axe or other implement of breaking up statues
	1 wand or spell of polymorph
	many monsters (must not be immune to stoning)

	Find yourself a cockatrice and slay it.  Wearing a pair of
gloves, pick up the corpse and wield it.  Be careful not to fall while
carrying it, as you will die if that happens.  A ring of levitation
could be useful for this, but is not necessary.  Find some monsters
and whack them over the head with the corpse.  Presto!  Instant
statues!  When you get bored or the corpse disintegrates, pile up all
the statues and polymorph them.  Some of them (10% or so) will become
boulders, but most will turn into other statues with the normal chance
of having spellbooks.  For added fun, separate out the rocks you've
generated and polymorph them into gems!

